table --> tbody --> tr 5th and td 1st --> which is pointing to my desired element
table xpath = //table[@id='customers']/tbody
//tr[5]/td[1]

Xpath —> 2types
Absolute ==> right from the html starting till the desired element “/“
Html/body/div[4]/input[3] —> it wont use any attributes for that element

Relative ==> “//“
//tagname[@attbiutetype=‘attributevalue’ and @attributetype=‘value2’]
//tagname[@attbiutetype=‘attributevalue’ or @attributetype=‘value2’]


//iput[@name=‘login-button’]

* :
Xpath : contains :
//tagname[contains(@atrtribute,’value’)]

//tagname[starts-with(@atrtribute,’value’)]

Text:
Exact match ==>
//tagname[text()=‘desired text’]
Partial text match ==-> contains : //tagname[contains(text(),’desired text’)]

Starting text —> starts-with
//tagname[starts-with(text(),’desired text’)]

identify 5th element: or any specific element:
1. index based operation we will use square brackets
(//tagname[@attribute=‘value’])[5]  ==> 5th element
2. position based operation
//tagname[@attribute=‘value’][position()=5] ==> 5th
3. last() function --> last element
//tagname[@attribute=‘value’][last()]
